ty.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYLay hands suddenly on no man, neither be partaker of other men's sins: keep thyself pure.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book5§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Drink no longer water, but use a little wine for thy stomach's sake and thine often infirmities.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book5§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^Some men's sins are open beforehand, going before to judgment; and some men they follow after.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhLikewise also the good works of some are manifest beforehand; and they that are otherwise cannot be hid.¦layout ªlast_verse